<Article
  title="One room, a lot of side hustles"
  description="Return to Aura. One beautiful room at a time."
  kicker="The story"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>Every Aura starts the same way: a finished room you can put on land you already have. Smooth polycarbonate in clear, mirror or tint, with warm wood inside. That room is the product. Everything else on this site is a different job for it.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What the room can be</RevealHeading>
  <p>As a room, it is a home extension, an office or a guest stay. On a hillside, it sits on helical piles with a polycarbonate floor lit from underneath and a big deck. Put a few together and you have a small eco resort, planned for Canada and Costa Rica.</p>
  <p>Turn one long wall into an aeroponic garden and it is Leaf Skywalker, a grow room. Put a standard atmospheric water generator on the roof and a short bottling line inside and it is Thirst Contact, pulling water from the sky and bottling it in the backyard. Same room, new job.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What you can do now</RevealHeading>
  <p>Join the waitlist. Aura is at the concept stage, so ordering is not open yet, but the waitlist gets you first in line when builds open. Curious how this site is built? The source is on <a href="https://github.com/kr8tiv-ai/aura-homes">GitHub</a>.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What comes later</RevealHeading>
  <p>Down the road, Aura rooms can join the Aura Network: grow rooms growing food for a free food network, and Thirst Contact units bottling water for a free water network, with owners paid to keep them running. It is a future expansion of the Aura network, and it is not open yet. The details are in <a href="/journal/free-food-and-water">its own note</a>.</p>
  <p>Want a room first? Start at <a href="/#shell">the room</a>. Curious about growing or water? <a href="/farms">Aura Farms</a> and <a href="/water">Thirst Contact</a> have the details.</p>
</Article>
